                        "glosses": [
                            "Emphasizing the observance of ritual or practice over the meaning; self-righteous, hypocritical."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c5a869fa-16cb-4555-a0d8-fb9db1fc8c63",
                                "sense_id": "325f2f2b-9eb3-3472-8de8-2b8856f30361",
                                "text": "Perhaps no man in the world had less than Douglas the pharisaical precision of Methodism; he was totally averse to their sudden and evanescent flights of enthusiasm, their frantic ravings of intemperate zeal in devotion, as if invoking a vindictive and implacable Deity;[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "75da1fd8-a35e-42e5-9322-67b516caa3ab",
                                "sense_id": "325f2f2b-9eb3-3472-8de8-2b8856f30361",
                                "text": "Thus Aurobindo Ghose stated that the puritanical, pharisaical British conquered in the name of liberty and usurped under the cloak of altruism."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
